      "message": "I think using param that way here and in other places may be dangerous and I think we should copy them in the first place and use the copy all way long.\n\nWhat I mean in this case:\n1) in line 247 we check `param-\u003edid \u003d\u003d FLPT_DEFAULT_DID`\nlater the host could change the params since it still accessed by host, so lets assume we go to line 259 and sets pgd to host provided one)\n2) in `set_context_entry` (after patch https://android-review.git.corp.google.com/c/kernel/common/+/3818903) the `param-\u003edid \u003d\u003d FLPT_DEFAULT_DID` is checked again but malicious host could change it so it will now use host provided `domain_pgd_gpa` (instead `pkvm_host_ept_pgd`) but `set_context_entry` will skip the domain presence verification and so one.\n\nI think there are other cases which could cause a security issue if the pramas could be changed by the malicious host in the middle. e.g. if params were change later on the  `context_present_cache_flush` could flush wrong bdf and so one?\n\nOr am I missing something?",
