      "side": 1,
      "message": "pv_param is a percpu variable and when host makes a hypercall it disables interrupt and preemption while using this pv_param. So it is guaranteed that the host cpu that invoked this hypercall is not accessing it until hypercall returns and host calls `put_this_pv_param()`.\n\nBut now when I think about it, another cpu might be able to access it if it choses to. So its a security gap I guess. Thanks for bringing this up. Its used in kvm hypercalls as well. @dmaluka@google.com, what do you think?\n\nI can have pkvm verion of get_pv_param and put_pv_param which takes a local pv_param variable and copy from and to to it(similar to kernel\u0027s copy_from_user/copy_to_user). Or probably unmap from host ept while pkvm is using it(but its heavyweight than copy)",
